@startuml sequence-session
' Dual session model: (1) Better Auth login session (2) anonymous browsing session
' Sources: SessionProvider, middleware.ts, browser-sequence-session.ts, sequence/_cookie.ts

title Session Persistence — Auth + Browsing\n(Legend: Two independent session keys)

skinparam sequenceMessageAlign center
skinparam ParticipantPadding 12

actor User as user
participant "Browser" as browser #LightBlue
participant "SessionProvider\nauthClient.useSession" as authSess #SkyBlue
participant "Better Auth\n/api/auth/get-session" as ba #Orange
participant "middleware.ts\n(matcher: /dashboard)" as mw #Pink
participant "localStorage\nsq_browser_session" as ls #Wheat
participant "Cookie sq_session\n(httpOnly)" as cookie #Wheat
participant "Sequence APIs\n/api/sequence/*" as seq #LightGreen
database "PostgreSQL" as pg #LightGreen

== A) Auth session (login persistence) ==

user -> browser : Load any page
browser -> authSess : Mount SessionProvider
authSess -> ba : useSession() → GET /api/auth/get-session\n(credentials: include)
ba -> pg : Validate session token (unless cookieCache hit)
ba --> authSess : { user, session } + customSession fields
authSess --> user : React context session

note over ba
  **cookieCache** enabled (5 min) in auth.ts —\nreduces DB reads for session enrichment.
end note

user -> browser : Email sign-in / OAuth complete
ba -> browser : Set Better Auth session cookie(s)
browser -> authSess : refetch() after login

== B) Middleware (optimistic /dashboard guard) ==

user -> browser : GET /dashboard
browser -> mw : Next.js middleware
mw -> mw : getSessionCookie(request)
alt no session cookie
  mw --> browser : 302 Redirect to /
else cookie present
  mw --> browser : NextResponse.next()\n(note: not fully secure per comment)
end

== C) Browsing / analytics session (guest or logged-in) ==

user -> browser : First visit storefront
browser -> ls : getOrCreateBrowserSequenceSessionId()\ncrypto.randomUUID() if missing
ls --> browser : session UUID

user -> seq : fetch POST + X-Sequence-Session header
seq -> cookie : resolveSequenceKey — sync sq_session cookie
seq -> pg : shopping_sequence / sales_micro_event rows

user -> browser : Tab close from /shop-details
browser -> seq : sendBeacon /api/sequence/end\n(cookie only, no custom header)
seq -> cookie : resolveSequenceKeyMaybe()
seq -> pg : endActiveSequenceIfVisitedProduct

note over ls, cookie
  **Two keys:** Better Auth cookies (login) vs `sq_browser_session` (funnel/telemetry).\nTelemetry may attach userId via cookie cache without full session DB read.
end note

@enduml
